Notice of the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, and the Ministry of Justice on Issuing the Opinions of the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, and the Ministry of Justice on Handling Criminal Cases of Drunk Dangerous Driving

Gao Jian Fa Ban Zi [2023] No. 187

To: All High People's Courts, People's Procuratorates, Public Security Departments (Bureaus), and Justice Departments (Bureaus) of provinces, autonomous regions, and municipalities directly under the Central Government; the Military Court of the People's Liberation Army, the Military Procuratorate of the People's Liberation Army, the Security Bureau of the Political and Legal Affairs Commission of the Central Military Commission; the Production and Construction Corps Branch of the High People's Court of Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region; the People's Procuratorate, Public Security Bureau, and Justice Bureau of the Xinjiang Production and Construction Corps:

Since the criminalization of drunk driving in 2011, all localities have adhered to strict law enforcement and impartial justice, lawfully punishing illegal and criminal acts of driving after drinking alcohol and drunk driving, effectively safeguarding the safety of people's lives and property and road traffic safety, and achieving significant results in the governance of driving after drinking alcohol and drunk driving. In order to adapt to new circumstances and new changes, further unify law enforcement and judicial standards, strictly regulate and lawfully handle drunk driving cases, the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, and the Ministry of Justice have formulated the Opinions on Handling Criminal Cases of Drunk Dangerous Driving, which are hereby issued to you for earnest implementation. Problems encountered during implementation shall be promptly reported level by level to the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, the Ministry of Public Security, and the Ministry of Justice.

December 13, 2023

Supreme People's Court, Supreme People's Procuratorate, Ministry of Public Security, Ministry of Justice

Opinions on Handling Criminal Cases of Drunk Dangerous Driving

In order to safeguard the safety of people's lives and property and road traffic safety, and to lawfully punish the illegal and criminal acts of drunk dangerous driving (hereinafter referred to as drunk driving), these Opinions are formulated in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Criminal Law, the Criminal Procedure Law, etc., and in light of law enforcement and judicial practice.

I. General Requirements

Article 1 People's courts, people's procuratorates, and public security organs handling drunk driving cases shall adhere to the principles of division of responsibilities, mutual cooperation, and mutual checks and balances, adhere to the correct application of law, adhere to the principle of trial based on evidence, strictly enforce the law, administer impartial justice, improve case handling efficiency, and achieve the organic unity of political effect, legal effect, and social effect. People's procuratorates shall carry out legal supervision over the handling activities of drunk driving cases in accordance with law.

Article 2 People's courts, people's procuratorates, and public security organs handling drunk driving cases shall comprehensively and accurately implement the criminal policy of combining leniency with severity, apply differential treatment according to the specific circumstances of the case, and achieve leniency where leniency is due, severity where severity is due, and punishment commensurate with the crime.

Article 3 People's courts, people's procuratorates, public security organs, and judicial administrative organs shall adhere to the combination of punishment and prevention, adopt multiple methods to strengthen comprehensive governance and source governance, and prevent and reduce the occurrence of driving after drinking alcohol from the source.

II. Case Filing and Investigation

Article 4 Where a person drives a motor vehicle on a road, and a breath alcohol content test shows a blood alcohol content of 80 mg/100 ml or more, the public security organ shall decide whether to file a case in accordance with the provisions of the Criminal Procedure Law and these Opinions. Where the circumstances are obviously minor, the harm is not great, and the act is not considered a crime, the case shall not be filed.

The public security organ shall promptly extract a blood sample from the criminal suspect for testing. Whether a criminal suspect is drunk shall be determined mainly based on the expert opinion on blood alcohol content.

Where a criminal suspect, after a breath alcohol content test showing a blood alcohol content of 80 mg/100 ml or more, escapes or arranges for another person to take the blame before the blood sample is extracted, the result of the breath alcohol content test may be used as the basis for determining his or her drunk state.

Where a criminal suspect, in order to evade legal liability, intentionally drinks alcohol before a breath alcohol content test or extraction of a blood sample during a lawful inspection by a public security organ or after a road traffic accident, the expert opinion on blood alcohol content obtained after the seizure may be used as the basis for determining his or her drunk state.

Article 5 The determination of "road" and "motor vehicle" in drunk driving cases shall apply the provisions of the Road Traffic Safety Law concerning "road" and "motor vehicle".

Whether a road section within the jurisdiction of an organ, enterprise, institution, factory, mine, campus, residential community, or other entity is determined as a "road" shall be judged based on whether it is "public" and whether it "allows the passage of social motor vehicles". Where only motor vehicles of the entity or specific visiting motor vehicles are allowed to pass, it may not be determined as a "road".

Article 6 A criminal suspect or defendant in a drunk driving case may, depending on the specific circumstances of the case, be detained or released on bail pending trial in accordance with law. Where any of the following circumstances exists, release on bail pending trial shall generally be granted:

(1) The person needs medical treatment due to personal injury;
(2) The person suffers from a serious illness and is not suitable for custody;
(3) The person is a pregnant woman or a woman nursing her own infant;
(4) The person is the sole supporter of a person who cannot take care of himself or herself;
(5) Other circumstances requiring release on bail pending trial.

Where the conditions for release on bail pending trial are met, but the criminal suspect or defendant cannot provide a guarantor nor pay the deposit, residential surveillance may be imposed. Where a criminal suspect or defendant violates the provisions on release on bail pending trial or residential surveillance, and the circumstances are serious, arrest may be made.

Article 7 When handling a drunk driving case, the following evidence shall be collected:

(1) Evidence materials proving the circumstances of the criminal suspect, mainly including identity documents such as population information inquiry records or household registration certificates; driver's license and driver information inquiry records; criminal record; records of being apprehended or subjected to administrative penalties for driving after drinking alcohol; the current administrative penalty decision for traffic violations, etc.;
(2) Evidence materials proving the situation of drunk detection and appraisal, mainly including the result of the breath alcohol content test, the calibration certificate of the breath alcohol content tester, the record of blood sample extraction, the appraisal entrustment letter or the registration materials for the appraisal institution receiving the test material, the expert opinion on blood alcohol content, the notice of expert opinion, etc.;
(3) Evidence materials proving the condition of the motor vehicle, mainly including the motor vehicle driving permit, motor vehicle information inquiry records, photographs of the motor vehicle, etc.;
(4) Photographs proving the scene of law enforcement, mainly including photographs of on-site inspection of the motor vehicle, breath alcohol content test, extraction and sealing of blood samples, etc., and audio and video recordings of the relevant steps shall be preserved;
(5) Confessions and defenses of the criminal suspect.

Depending on the specific circumstances of the case, the following evidence shall also be collected:

(1) Where there is a dispute as to whether the criminal suspect drank alcohol or drove a motor vehicle, witness testimony from persons in the same vehicle, eyewitnesses at the scene, or persons who drank alcohol together, surveillance recordings of the place of drinking and the section of road traveled, etc., shall be collected;
(2) Where there is a dispute as to the attribute of the road, testimony from knowledgeable persons such as relevant management personnel and owners, certificates issued by the management unit or relevant departments, etc., shall be collected;
(3) Where a traffic accident has occurred, the traffic accident identification certificate, surveillance recordings of the accident section, expert opinions on the degree of human injury, statements of the victim, etc., shall be collected;
(4) Where surrender may be established, materials such as the record of the criminal suspect's arrival at the case shall be collected;
(5) Other evidence materials truly necessary to be collected.

Article 8 The procedures for extraction, sealing, storage, submission for testing, and appraisal of blood samples from criminal suspects shall be carried out in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Ministry of Public Security and the Ministry of Justice on procedures for handling road traffic safety illegal acts and appraisal rules.

The process of extraction and sealing of blood samples by the public security organ shall be fully recorded by audio and video. The extraction and sealing of blood samples shall be marked and numbered, and the extractor, sealer, and criminal suspect shall sign the record of blood sample extraction. Where the criminal suspect refuses to sign, this shall be noted. The extracted blood samples shall be promptly sent to an appraisal institution for blood alcohol content appraisal. Where submission for testing cannot be promptly made due to special reasons, the test material shall be stored in accordance with relevant norms and technical standards and submitted for testing within five working days.

The appraisal institution shall conduct audio and video recording of the blood sample preparation and instrument testing process. The appraisal institution shall, within three working days after receiving the blood sample submitted for testing, conduct the appraisal and issue the expert opinion on blood alcohol content in accordance with relevant norms and technical standards, and notify or deliver it to the entrusting unit.

Where the expert opinion on blood alcohol content is used as evidence, the case-handling unit shall, within five working days from the date of receiving the expert opinion on blood alcohol content, notify the criminal suspect, defendant, victim, or their legal representative in writing.

Article 9 Where any of the following circumstances exists, and the defect is cured or a reasonable explanation is provided, the expert opinion on blood alcohol content may be used as the basis for adjudication; where the defect cannot be cured or a reasonable explanation cannot be provided, it shall be excluded:

(1) The extraction, sealing, or storage of the blood sample is not in conformity with the rules;
(2) The submission for testing or issuance of the expert opinion is not carried out in accordance with the prescribed time and procedure;
(3) The appraisal process is not recorded by audio and video in accordance with the provisions;
(4) Other defects or irregular evidence collection acts exist.

III. Criminal Liability

Article 10 Where drunk driving has any of the following circumstances and does not yet constitute another crime, a heavier punishment shall be imposed:

(1) Causing a traffic accident and bearing full or primary responsibility for the accident;
(2) Fleeing after causing a traffic accident;
(3) Driving a motor vehicle without obtaining a motor vehicle driver's license;
(4) Driving with serious overcrowding, overloading, or overspeeding;
(5) Driving after taking psychotropic drugs or narcotic drugs regulated by the state;
(6) Driving a motor vehicle engaged in passenger transport activities with passengers on board;
(7) Driving a motor vehicle engaged in school bus operations with teachers and students on board;
(8) Driving on a highway;
(9) Driving a heavy-duty cargo vehicle;
(10) Transporting dangerous chemicals or dangerous goods;
(11) Evading or obstructing a lawful inspection by a public security organ;
(12) Engaging in acts of intimidating, retaliating against, inducing, or bribing witnesses, appraisers, or other persons, or destroying or falsifying evidence, or other acts obstructing the administration of justice;
(13) Having been apprehended or subjected to administrative penalties for driving after drinking alcohol within the past two years;
(14) Having been convicted or given a relative non-prosecution for dangerous driving within the past five years;
(15) Other circumstances requiring a heavier punishment.

Article 11 Where drunk driving has any of the following circumstances, a lenient punishment shall be imposed:

(1) Voluntary surrender, confession, or meritorious service;
(2) Voluntary admission of guilt and acceptance of punishment;
(3) Causing a traffic accident, compensating for losses, or obtaining forgiveness;
(4) Other circumstances requiring a lenient punishment.

Article 12 Where drunk driving has any of the following circumstances and does not have any of the circumstances provided in Article 10 of these Opinions, it may be determined that the circumstances are obviously minor, the harm is not great, and the case shall be handled in accordance with Article 13 of the Criminal Law and Article 16 of the Criminal Procedure Law:

(1) The blood alcohol content is less than 150 mg/100 ml;
(2) Driving a motor vehicle due to an emergency situation such as rescuing a sick or injured person, and the act does not constitute necessity;
(3) Driving a motor vehicle over a short distance in a residential community, parking lot, or other place for purposes such as moving the vehicle or parking;
(4) Driving a motor vehicle over a short distance in a residential community, parking lot, or other place to take over parking from another person, or driving out of a residential community, parking lot, or other place over a short distance to hand over the vehicle to another person for driving;
(5) Other circumstances where the circumstances are obviously minor.

Where, after drinking alcohol, a person is compelled to drive a motor vehicle due to an emergency situation such as rescuing a sick or injured person, and the act constitutes necessity, the case shall be handled in accordance with Article 21 of the Criminal Law.

Article 13 In a drunk driving case transferred by a public security organ for examination and prosecution, where the people's procuratorate comprehensively considers factors such as the motive and purpose of driving, the degree of intoxication, the type of motor vehicle, road conditions, time, speed, and distance of driving, and the manifestation of admission of guilt and remorse, and finds that the circumstances of the crime are minor, the case shall be handled in accordance with Article 37 of the Criminal Law and Article 177, paragraph 2, of the Criminal Procedure Law.

Article 14 For a defendant in a drunk driving case who meets the conditions provided in Article 72 of the Criminal Law, a suspended sentence shall be declared in accordance with law. Where any of the following circumstances exists, a suspended sentence shall generally not be applied:

(1) Causing a traffic accident resulting in minor or light injuries to others, and bearing full or primary responsibility for the accident;
(2) Causing a traffic accident and bearing full or primary responsibility for the accident, but failing to compensate for losses;
(3) Fleeing after causing a traffic accident;
(4) Driving a motor vehicle without obtaining a motor vehicle driver's license;
(5) Blood alcohol content exceeding 180 mg/100 ml;
(6) Driving after taking psychotropic drugs or narcotic drugs regulated by the state;
(7) Using violent means to resist a lawful inspection by a public security organ, or committing acts obstructing the administration of justice;
(8) Having been apprehended or subjected to administrative penalties for driving after drinking alcohol within the past five years;
(9) Having been convicted or given a relative non-prosecution for dangerous driving;
(10) Other circumstances where the circumstances are heinous.

Article 15 When imposing a fine on a defendant, the amount of the fine shall be determined in accordance with the criminal circumstances such as the drunk driving act and actual damage consequences, and taking into consideration the defendant's ability to pay the fine, so as to be commensurate with the principal punishment. The starting point for the fine shall generally not be lower than the amount of the fine for the corresponding circumstance of driving after drinking alcohol provided in the Road Traffic Safety Law; for each additional month of criminal detention, the fine shall be increased by RMB 1,000 to RMB 5,000.

Article 16 Where drunk driving simultaneously constitutes another crime such as the crime of causing a traffic accident, the crime of negligently endangering public safety by dangerous means, or the crime of endangering public safety by dangerous means, the conviction shall be based on the provision providing for the heavier punishment, and criminal liability shall be pursued strictly in accordance with law.

Where a person drives a motor vehicle while drunk, uses violence or threats to obstruct a lawful inspection by a public security organ, and further constitutes another crime such as the crime of obstructing public service or the crime of assaulting the police, the punishment shall be imposed in accordance with the provisions on concurrent punishment for multiple crimes.

Article 17 Where a criminal suspect, after being apprehended at the scene for drunk driving, is allowed to leave and then arrives at the case upon notification by the public security organ or voluntarily, this shall not be considered voluntary surrender; where after causing a traffic accident, the suspect protects the scene, rescues the injured, reports to the public security organ, and cooperates with the investigation, this shall be considered voluntary surrender.

Article 18 In cases handled in accordance with Article 12, paragraph 1, Article 13, and Article 14 of these Opinions, the circumstances of the criminal suspect or defendant voluntarily accepting safe driving education, engaging in traffic volunteer service, and participating in community public service may be taken into consideration as factors in making the relevant decisions.

Article 19 Where a decision is made not to prosecute a criminal suspect or to exempt a defendant from criminal punishment, depending on the different circumstances of the case, the person may be admonished or ordered to sign a statement of repentance, apologize, or compensate for losses; where administrative penalties or sanctions need to be imposed, the case shall be transferred to the relevant competent authority for handling.

Article 20 Drunk driving is a serious act of driving after drinking alcohol. Where the blood alcohol content reaches 80 mg/100 ml or more, the public security organ shall, before deciding not to file a case, dismissing the case, or transferring the case for examination and prosecution, impose the administrative penalty of revoking the motor vehicle driver's license on the actor. In cases handled in accordance with Article 12, paragraph 1, of these Opinions, the public security organ shall also impose the administrative penalties of a fine and administrative detention on the actor in accordance with the corresponding circumstances of driving after drinking alcohol provided in the Road Traffic Safety Law.

Where a people's court or people's procuratorate handles a case in accordance with Article 12, paragraph 1, or Article 13 of these Opinions, and administrative penalties need to be imposed on the person not prosecuted or the defendant, a procuratorial opinion or judicial suggestion shall be issued and the case shall be transferred to the public security organ for handling in accordance with the preceding paragraph. The public security organ shall notify the people's court and the people's procuratorate of the handling situation.

IV. Expedited Handling

Article 21 People's courts, people's procuratorates, public security organs, and judicial administrative organs shall strengthen cooperation and coordination, and, under the premise of following legal procedures and protecting the rights of the parties, establish and improve an expedited handling mechanism for drunk driving cases according to local conditions, simplify case handling procedures, shorten case handling time limits, and achieve high-quality and efficient handling of drunk driving cases.

Article 22 Drunk driving cases meeting the following conditions shall generally be handled through the expedited handling mechanism:

(1) The case is apprehended at the scene and does not cause a traffic accident;
(2) The facts are clear, the evidence is reliable and sufficient, and there is no dispute over the application of law;
(3) The criminal suspect or defendant voluntarily admits guilt and accepts punishment;
(4) The case does not have any of the circumstances provided in Article 223 of the Criminal Procedure Law.

Article 23 In a drunk driving case handled through the expedited handling mechanism, the people's court, people's procuratorate, and public security organ shall generally complete the investigation, prosecution, and trial within 30 days from the date of filing the case for investigation.

Article 24 Where the measure of release on bail pending trial is adopted during the investigation or examination and prosecution stage, and the case is transferred to the examination and prosecution or trial stage with the period of release on bail pending trial not yet expired and the conditions for release on bail pending trial still met, the receiving authority may not make a new decision on release on bail pending trial, and the public security organ shall continue to enforce the original measure of release on bail pending trial.

Article 25 Where a sentencing recommendation for a suspended sentence or a declaration of a suspended sentence is proposed for a defendant in a drunk driving case, an investigation and assessment may generally not be conducted. Where truly necessary, a community correction institution or relevant social organization shall be entrusted in a timely manner to conduct an investigation and assessment. The entrusted party shall promptly provide the investigation and assessment results to the entrusting authority.

Article 26 In drunk driving cases applying the summary procedure or the speedy procedure, the people's court, people's procuratorate, public security organ, and judicial administrative organ may adopt consolidated, essential, or tabular forms to simplify documents.

In areas where conditions permit, electronic case files and legal documents may be transmitted and served through an integrated online case handling platform to achieve online case handling.

V. Comprehensive Governance

Article 27 People's courts, people's procuratorates, public security organs, and judicial administrative organs shall actively implement the responsibility for legal popularization, strengthen legal education on road traffic safety, and extensively carry out legal popularization activities in government organs, villages, communities, schools, enterprises, units, and on the internet, guiding the public to cultivate a sense of rules and develop law-abiding habits.

Article 28 People's courts, people's procuratorates, public security organs, and judicial administrative organs shall fully utilize mechanisms such as judicial suggestions, procuratorial suggestions, and reminder letters to urge relevant departments, enterprises, and institutions to strengthen the education and management of their personnel, increase safe driving education in driver training sessions, regulate the development of the designated driving industry, strengthen the management of places involving alcohol such as restaurants and entertainment venues, and increase the intensity of warnings and reminders.

Article 29 Public security organs and judicial administrative organs shall, based on the specific circumstances of persons serving sentences for drunk driving and persons under community correction, formulate targeted education, reform, and correction plans, achieve classified management and individualized education, enhance their sense of remorse and legal concepts, and help them become law-abiding citizens.

VI. Supplementary Provisions

Article 30 These Opinions shall come into effect on December 28, 2023. The Opinions of the Supreme People's Court, the Supreme People's Procuratorate, and the Ministry of Public Security on Several Issues Concerning the Application of Law in Handling Criminal Cases of Drunk Driving Motor Vehicles (Fa Fa [2013] No. 15) shall be simultaneously abolished.
